-- title:
--   Regularity at non-∞ floor cusps of the pole chart, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity for which some ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq\operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) $q\,M'$, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $A\to K$ compatible via $L$; let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A$ and $f\cdot y=x$ in $\operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ (the Gauss ring). Put $B=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L144) $A\,K\,j$, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$. Then for every prime ideal $y$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$, containing $j^{-1}$, and containing $B\cap\mathfrak{m}_{W_0}$ (all $b\in B$ whose image in $K$ is a nonunit of $W_0$), and such that it is *not* the case that for all $b\in B$ whose Laurent series lies in the $L$-base change of [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305) $(q^2M')$ (the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the expansions $j(q^d)$ for $d\mid q^2M'$) one has $b\in y$ if and only if the $0$-th coefficient of $b$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_A$: any localisation $B_m$ of $B$ at $y$ is a regular local ring, and so is $B_m$ modulo the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$.
--
--   This is the regularity-with-regular-fibre statement at the cusps lying on the $\infty$-branch of the pole chart of the integral model of $X_H(q^2M')$ over $A$, in the case where the cusp lies over a cusp of the floor curve $X_0(q^2M')$ other than $\infty$; it is the $q=2$ companion of the corresponding statement for $q\ge 5$. It feeds the assembly of regularity along the Gauss-nonunits locus on the same branch, en route to semistability of the covering used for the level-lowering arguments.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_of_not_forall_mem_floor_iff_xH_of_isAlgebraic_of_eq_two.lean

